ves [[Cookbook:Red onion|red onion]], sliced 0.5 cm thick\n* 3 cm [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]], peeled and [[Cookbook:Mincing|minced]]\n* 2 red [[Cookbook:Chiles|chillies]], minced\n* 400 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] [[Cookbook:Beef|hamburger meat]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Scallion|scallion]], cut into 1 cm pieces\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Celery|celery]] stalks, minced\n* 600 g cooked [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Pepper|black pepper]]\n* 2 tbsp black [[Cookbook:Soy sauce|soy sauce]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Heat the canola oil in a [[Cookbook:Non-stick|non-stick]] [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|frying pan]]. When the oil is very hot, fry the garlic, red onion, ginger, and red chillies. Stir every 20 seconds until fragrant.\n# Add the hamburger meat, and cook until the meat browns and is cooked through.\n# Add the celery and scallion. Add the rice, salt, black pepper, and black soy sauce. Cook until well mixed and heated through.\n# Serve hot.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for fried rice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Inexpensive recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using canola oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green onion]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Hamburger Fried Rice","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"3","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"3 tbsp canola oil for frying","sourceText":"3 tbsp canola oil for frying","amountText":"3 tbsp canola oil for frying","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"4 cloves garlic, sliced 0.5 cm thick","sourceText":"4 cloves garlic, sliced 0.5 cm thick","amountText":"4 cloves garlic, sliced 0.5 cm thick","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"4 cloves red onion, sliced 0.5 cm thick","sourceText":"4 cloves red onion, sl